{
  "label": "not_comparable",
  "factor": "outcome_definition",
  "rationale": "The two selected claims do not share an identifiable comparable contrast. Side A's claim reports the main between-group association: sitagliptin use vs a matched control cohort in T2DM patients with ESRD on dialysis, with higher HHF incidence in the sitagliptin cohort (adjusted HR 1.52, 95% CI 1.21-1.90; assertion 'directional', estimate_direction '+'). Side B's selected claim does not report that main sitagliptin-vs-placebo hHF contrast; its outcome field is 'heterogeneity of the effect of sitagliptin on hHF across prespecified subgroups', its comparison.type is 'unclear', its estimate_direction is null, and its result rests on interaction testing ('P > .10 for all interactions'). An interaction/heterogeneity result is not evidence for the main contrast, so it cannot be placed against Side A's overall between-group effect estimate. Both extractions are faithful to their own sources (no material extraction error): the obstacle is that the selected estimands differ - a main-effect association on HHF incidence versus homogeneity of effect across subgroups - even though the same drug and a related outcome are involved. (Abstract B does contain an overall no-effect result, HR 1.00 and the conclusion that sitagliptin does not affect hHF risk, but that overall finding is not the selected claim.)",
  "diagnostics": {
    "material_extraction_error": false,
    "error_sides": [],
    "error_fields": [],
    "uncertain_extraction": false,
    "comparison_sufficient": false,
    "source_evidence": [
      {
        "side": "a",
        "sentence_id": 4,
        "quote": "The overall incidence of HHF was higher in the sitagliptin cohort than in the control cohort (1130 vs. 754 per 10000 person-years; adjusted hazard ratio (HR): 1.52, 95% CI = 1.21-1.90)."
      },
      {
        "side": "b",
        "sentence_id": 17,
        "quote": "No heterogeneity for the effect of sitagliptin on hHF was observed in subgroup analyses across 21 factors (P > .10 for all interactions)."
      },
      {
        "side": "b",
        "sentence_id": 19,
        "quote": "Sitagliptin use does not affect the risk for hHF in T2DM, both overall and among high-risk patient subgroups."
      }
    ]
  ,
    "notes": "Side A verification: claim matches sentences 2-4 and 7 (population T2DM+ESRD on dialysis, matched control cohort 1:4, multivariable Cox, significant adjusted HR 1.52). Side B verification: claim matches sentences 10, 13, 17 and 19 (TECOS RCT, 7332 sitagliptin vs 7339 placebo, subgroup interaction analyses, explicit no-heterogeneity wording); no field contradicts its source, so this is not a material extraction error. The decisive comparability obstacle is the differing estimand: Side B's selected claim targets subgroup interaction tests (comparison.type 'unclear', no main-effect direction), which per the retained target of statistical details cannot serve as evidence for the main sitagliptin-vs-control hHF contrast reported in Side A. Had Side B's overall hHF result (HR 1.00, 95% CI 0.83-1.19, with the explicit conclusion of no effect on hHF risk) been the selected claim, the pair would have supported a not_replicated comparison, with a text-supported population difference (ESRD on dialysis vs T2DM with prevalent atherosclerotic vascular disease) available as a contextual factor."
  }
}
